<title>DUBAI: Dubai Jan-March gold imports reach 154.90 T - WGC.</title>
<headline>Dubai Jan-March gold imports reach 154.90 T - WGC.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold imports into Dubai reached 154.90 tonnes in the first quarter of 1997, up from 74.97 tonnes the same period last year, the World Gold Council based in Dubai said on Monday.</p>
<p>The main supplier in the first quarter of 1997 was Switzerland with 109.25 tonnes, followed by Britain with 34.41 tonnes and South Africa with 8.28 tonnes, it added.</p>
<p>The council said first quarter imports into Singapore, Dubai's main gold market rival, were 135.7 tonnes.  </p>
<p>WGC said the sharp rise in imports to Dubai was largely due to strong Indian demand, which had been fanned by weak bullion prices.</p>
<p>Eighty five percent of the gold imported into Dubai goes to India.</p>
</text>
